import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Derived-Artifact Cache and Compression","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Derived-Artifact Cache and Compression","type":"adr","date":"2026-09-02T00:00:00.000Z","status":"proposed","status_note":"Proposed\\n\\nDepends on [ADR-0063 — Scheme-Core Completeness](./0063-scheme-core-completeness.md)\\nand [ADR-0064 — Computational Language Authoring](./0064-computational-language-authoring.md).\\nRefines [ADR-0044 — Language as Data and Runtime\\nSplit](./0044-language-as-data-and-runtime-split.md) §6 (fragment sources and\\nkit assembly)."},"headers":[],"relativePath":"handl/project/adrs/0065-derived-artifact-cache-and-compression.md","filePath":"vendored/handl/project/adrs/0065-derived-artifact-cache-and-compression.md"}`),a={name:`handl/project/adrs/0065-derived-artifact-cache-and-compression.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="adr-0065-derived-artifact-cache-and-compression" tabindex="-1">ADR-0065: Derived-Artifact Cache and Compression <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-0065-derived-artifact-cache-and-compression" aria-label="Permalink to “ADR-0065: Derived-Artifact Cache and Compression”">​</a></h1><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to “Context”">​</a></h2><p>ADR-0044 §6 made authored data files canonical and embedded them at compile time via <code>include_str!</code>. This is compile-time caching: zero runtime parse cost, zero I/O. It works for the canonical kit and any kit known at build time.</p><p>It does not cover <strong>runtime-loaded languages</strong>. Once handl can author <code>Language</code> values computationally (ADR-0064) and self-describe (ADR-0063), languages can be loaded at runtime — user-defined kits, mods, dynamically generated dialects. Each load requires:</p><ol><li>Read the authoring source (handl program or YAML).</li><li>If handl: <code>eval</code> the authoring program to produce fragment values.</li><li>Merge fragments in kit-defined order (ADR-0044 §1, §5).</li><li>Resolve <code>replaces</code> override chains (ADR-0044 §5).</li><li>Validate <code>requires</code> dependencies (ADR-0044 §7).</li><li>Build the merged <code>Language</code> value.</li></ol><p>Steps 2–6 are deterministic given the same inputs. Repeating them on every load is wasted work. This is where caching applies.</p><h3 id="the-danger-stale-cache-silent-semantic-drift" tabindex="-1">The danger: stale cache = silent semantic drift <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-danger-stale-cache-silent-semantic-drift" aria-label="Permalink to “The danger: stale cache = silent semantic drift”">​</a></h3><p>ADR-0044 §5 makes composition an <strong>auditable override graph</strong>: fragments declare <code>replaces: [id]</code>, and the merged <code>Language</code> carries the full history of what replaced what. A cache that serves a stale merged <code>Language</code> — one that does not reflect a change in a fragment source, a kit manifest, an <code>extends</code> chain, or an engine selection — produces <strong>silent semantic drift</strong>. The program runs under a language that is not the one the author intended, with no error. &quot;Why does this <code>let</code> parse differently?&quot; is answerable by reading the override chain (ADR-0044 §5) — unless the cache served a stale chain.</p><p>This is the dangerous failure mode, not a crash. A crash is recoverable; silent drift is not. The cache key must be correct, or the cache must not exist.</p><h3 id="compression-modest-secondary" tabindex="-1">Compression: modest, secondary <a class="header-anchor" href="#compression-modest-secondary" aria-label="Permalink to “Compression: modest, secondary”">​</a></h3><p>The canonical <code>Language</code> is ~180KB of YAML. Compressed (zstd, level 3–9), ~30–40KB. This is a real win for binary size and runtime I/O on constrained targets, but it is not a motivation on its own. Compression is a property of the cached artifact, not a feature.</p><p>The constraint: <strong>compress the derived artifact, never the authored source.</strong> ADR-0044 §1 claims <code>Language</code> is &quot;inspectable, authorable as text.&quot; Compressing the authored source (YAML or handl program) breaks that property. The authored source stays text; the serialized merged <code>Language</code> (the cache payload) may be compressed.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to “Decision”">​</a></h2><h3 id="_1-cache-the-merged-language-not-the-authoring-source" tabindex="-1">1. Cache the merged <code>Language</code>, not the authoring source <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-cache-the-merged-language-not-the-authoring-source" aria-label="Permalink to “1. Cache the merged Language, not the authoring source”">​</a></h3><p>The cache stores the <strong>output of the assembly pipeline</strong>: the merged, validated <code>Language</code> value, serialized (serde). The input is the full set of fragment sources + kit manifest + <code>extends</code> chain + engine selections. The cache does not store intermediate fragments or the authoring program; it stores the final product.</p><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>cache key → serialized merged Language (optionally compressed)</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id="_2-cache-key-is-a-hash-of-the-full-assembly-input" tabindex="-1">2. Cache key is a hash of the full assembly input <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-cache-key-is-a-hash-of-the-full-assembly-input" aria-label="Permalink to “2. Cache key is a hash of the full assembly input”">​</a></h3><p>The cache key is a cryptographic hash (BLAKE3) of a canonical serialization of:</p><ol><li>Every fragment source (YAML file content hash, or handl program content hash + the <code>Language</code> used to eval it).</li><li>The kit manifest (ordered fragment-source list + include/exclude filters).</li><li>The <code>extends</code> chain (transitive: parent kits&#39; manifests, recursively).</li><li>Engine selections (lex/parse/eval engine names + versions, per ADR-0044 §7 &quot;Engine selection as data&quot;).</li><li>The <code>scheme_version</code> declared by the <code>Language</code> (ADR-0044 §7).</li></ol><p>If any input changes, the hash changes, and the cache misses. This is the only correct cache key. Hashing a subset (e.g., only the top-level manifest) risks stale hits when a transitive dependency changes.</p><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>key = blake3(canonical_serialize(</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    fragment_source_hashes,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    kit_manifest,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    extends_chain_transitive,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    engine_selections,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    scheme_version,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>))</span></span></code></pre></div><h3 id="_3-compression-is-applied-to-the-cache-payload-not-the-source" tabindex="-1">3. Compression is applied to the cache payload, not the source <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-compression-is-applied-to-the-cache-payload-not-the-source" aria-label="Permalink to “3. Compression is applied to the cache payload, not the source”">​</a></h3><p>The serialized merged <code>Language</code> is compressed with zstd before storage. Decompression happens on cache hit. The authored source (YAML, handl program) is never compressed by this system — it remains text on disk.</p><p>Compression level is configurable. Default: level 3 (fast, ~2x compression). Constrained targets may use level 9 (~4x, slower decompression). The tradeoff is I/O cost vs CPU cost, and it is a runtime config, not a build decision.</p><h3 id="_4-cache-invalidation-is-by-key-not-by-ttl" tabindex="-1">4. Cache invalidation is by key, not by TTL <a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-cache-invalidation-is-by-key-not-by-ttl" aria-label="Permalink to “4. Cache invalidation is by key, not by TTL”">​</a></h3><p>There is no time-based expiry. The cache is valid as long as the key matches. If the assembly input changes, the key changes, and the old entry is a miss (not a stale hit). This is correct because the assembly is a pure function of its inputs — same inputs, same output; different inputs, different output.</p><p>TTL-based invalidation is explicitly rejected: it introduces a window where the cache is stale but the key has not changed (e.g., a file was edited but the TTL has not expired). This is the silent-drift failure mode.</p><h3 id="_5-cache-storage-is-pluggable" tabindex="-1">5. Cache storage is pluggable <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-cache-storage-is-pluggable" aria-label="Permalink to “5. Cache storage is pluggable”">​</a></h3><p>The cache backend is a trait, not a fixed implementation:</p><div class="language-rust"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">rust</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-dark:#0F0;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;">pub</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#0F0;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;"> trait</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#6F42C1;"> LanguageCache</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-light:#24292E;"> {</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-dark:#0F0;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;">    fn</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#6F42C1;"> get</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-light:#24292E;">(</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#0FF;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;">&amp;</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#0FF;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;">self</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-light:#24292E;">,</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#24292E;"> key</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;">:</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#0FF;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;"> &amp;</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#6F42C1;">CacheKey</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-light:#24292E;">)</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#0F0;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;"> -&gt;</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#6F42C1;"> Option</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-light:#24292E;">&lt;</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#6F42C1;">CachedLanguage</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-light:#24292E;">&gt;;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-dark:#0F0;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;">    fn</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#6F42C1;"> put</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-light:#24292E;">(</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#0FF;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;">&amp;</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#0FF;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;">self</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-light:#24292E;">,</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#24292E;"> key</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;">:</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#0FF;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;"> &amp;</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#6F42C1;">CacheKey</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-light:#24292E;">,</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#24292E;"> lang</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;">:</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#0FF;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;"> &amp;</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#6F42C1;">CachedLanguage</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-light:#24292E;">)</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#0F0;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic;--shiki-light:#c62739;--shiki-light-font-style:inherit;"> -&gt;</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#FFFFFF;--shiki-light:#6F42C1;"> Result</span><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-light:#24292E;">&lt;()&gt;;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-dark:#888888;--shiki-light:#24292E;">}</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Implementations:</p><ul><li><code>NoCache</code> — always misses (default for compile-time-embedded kits).</li><li><code>InMemoryCache</code> — <code>HashMap&lt;CacheKey, CachedLanguage&gt;</code>, process-lifetime.</li><li><code>OnDiskCache</code> — files in a cache directory, persistent across runs.</li><li>(future) <code>NetworkCache</code> — shared cache for a fleet of hosts.</li></ul><h3 id="_6-compile-time-embedding-remains-the-primary-path" tabindex="-1">6. Compile-time embedding remains the primary path <a class="header-anchor" href="#_6-compile-time-embedding-remains-the-primary-path" aria-label="Permalink to “6. Compile-time embedding remains the primary path”">​</a></h3><p>For the canonical kit and any kit known at build time, <code>include_str!</code> + compile-time assembly remains the path. The cache is for <strong>runtime-loaded</strong> languages only. A compile-time-embedded <code>Language</code> is already &quot;cached&quot; in the binary; the runtime cache adds nothing.</p><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to “Consequences”">​</a></h2><h3 id="positive" tabindex="-1">Positive <a class="header-anchor" href="#positive" aria-label="Permalink to “Positive”">​</a></h3><ul><li><strong>Runtime-loaded languages are fast on repeat loads.</strong> The first load assembles; subsequent loads with the same inputs hit the cache. This makes mods, user-defined kits, and dynamic dialects practical.</li><li><strong>No silent drift.</strong> The cache key includes every input that affects the merged <code>Language</code>. A change in any input is a guaranteed cache miss.</li><li><strong>Compression reduces I/O and binary size for cached artifacts.</strong> Modest but real, especially for constrained targets or network-loaded languages.</li><li><strong>The authored source stays inspectable.</strong> Compression applies only to the derived artifact; the source remains text.</li></ul><h3 id="negative" tabindex="-1">Negative <a class="header-anchor" href="#negative" aria-label="Permalink to “Negative”">​</a></h3><ul><li><strong>Cache key computation has a cost.</strong> Hashing every fragment source on every load is not free. For a small kit, this may exceed the cost of re-assembling. The cache is a win only when assembly is more expensive than key computation — which is true for computationally authored languages (ADR-0064) but may not be for small YAML kits.</li><li><strong>The cache backend is a new subsystem.</strong> Trait + implementations + storage management + eviction (for <code>OnDiskCache</code>). This is real infrastructure, not a wrapper.</li><li><strong>Correctness depends on the key being complete.</strong> A missing input in the key (e.g., forgetting to include the <code>scheme_version</code>) is a stale-hit bug. The key construction is the crux; it must be audited carefully.</li></ul><h3 id="neutral" tabindex="-1">Neutral <a class="header-anchor" href="#neutral" aria-label="Permalink to “Neutral”">​</a></h3><ul><li><strong>No TTL.</strong> This is by design. The cache is a pure-function memoization, not a freshness system. If freshness is needed (e.g., &quot;reload if the source file changed&quot;), it is handled by detecting the source change and computing a new key, not by expiring the old one.</li></ul><h2 id="implementation-phases" tabindex="-1">Implementation phases <a class="header-anchor" href="#implementation-phases" aria-label="Permalink to “Implementation phases”">​</a></h2><h3 id="phase-1-—-languagecache-trait-and-nocache-inmemorycache" tabindex="-1">Phase 1 — <code>LanguageCache</code> trait and <code>NoCache</code>/<code>InMemoryCache</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#phase-1-—-languagecache-trait-and-nocache-inmemorycache" aria-label="Permalink to “Phase 1 — LanguageCache trait and NoCache/InMemoryCache”">​</a></h3><p>Define the trait and the two simple implementations. <code>NoCache</code> is the default. <code>InMemoryCache</code> is opt-in. No compression yet.</p><h3 id="phase-2-—-cache-key-construction" tabindex="-1">Phase 2 — Cache key construction <a class="header-anchor" href="#phase-2-—-cache-key-construction" aria-label="Permalink to “Phase 2 — Cache key construction”">​</a></h3><p>Implement the BLAKE3 key over the full assembly input. Test: every input change produces a different key; same inputs produce the same key. This is the correctness-critical piece.</p><h3 id="phase-3-—-ondiskcache-with-zstd-compression" tabindex="-1">Phase 3 — <code>OnDiskCache</code> with zstd compression <a class="header-anchor" href="#phase-3-—-ondiskcache-with-zstd-compression" aria-label="Permalink to “Phase 3 — OnDiskCache with zstd compression”">​</a></h3><p>Add the persistent backend with compression. Test: cache survives process restart; compressed payload decompresses to the correct <code>Language</code>.</p><h3 id="phase-4-—-integration-with-runtime-kit-loading" tabindex="-1">Phase 4 — Integration with runtime kit loading <a class="header-anchor" href="#phase-4-—-integration-with-runtime-kit-loading" aria-label="Permalink to “Phase 4 — Integration with runtime kit loading”">​</a></h3><p>Wire the cache into the runtime&#39;s kit-assembly path. A kit load checks the cache; on miss, assembles and stores; on hit, loads the cached <code>Language</code>. The compile-time-embedded path bypasses the cache entirely.</p><h2 id="references" tabindex="-1">References <a class="header-anchor" href="#references" aria-label="Permalink to “References”">​</a></h2><ul><li><a href="./0063-scheme-core-completeness.html">ADR-0063</a> — Scheme-Core Completeness (the cache stores a <code>Language</code> value; that value must be complete)</li><li><a href="./0064-computational-language-authoring.html">ADR-0064</a> — Computational Language Authoring (the primary consumer; computationally authored languages benefit most from caching)</li><li><a href="./0044-language-as-data-and-runtime-split.html">ADR-0044</a> — Language as Data and Runtime Split (§5 override graph is the silent-drift risk; §6 fragment sources; §7 engine selection as data)</li><li><a href="./0046-capability-discipline-at-the-language-level.html">ADR-0046</a> — Capability Discipline (cached <code>Language</code> values carry their capability set; the cache does not bypass capability checks)</li></ul>`,52)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};